Name: wayland
URL: http://wayland.freedesktop.org/
Version: 1.26.0
Revision: 87cc8a8728a923fc57938faa81ba0e74f34ecdc7
Update Mechanism: Autoroll
CPEPrefix: cpe:/a:wayland:wayland:1.20.91
License: MIT
License File: src/COPYING
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Description:
Wayland is a protocol for a compositor to talk to its clients as well as a C
library implementation of that protocol.

Note: It appears that Wayland has been failing to register CPEs with
nvd.nist.gov. Thus the last actual CPEPrefix is 1.20.91, even though newer
versions exist.

Modifications:
- Added wayland_scanner_wrapper.py to generate protocol code automatically.
- Added "include/" include_dirs for the wayland_server target
- Added automatic generation of protocol marshalling code.
- Made server/client generated with wayland_protocol template.
- Added generate_configs.py that generates config.h into include/. It
  removes PACKAGE_VERSION, which libwayland doesn't use, so config.h doesn't
  depend on the libwayland version.
- wayland-version.h is generated at build time from the upstream template and
  src/meson.build (generate_version_header.py).
- wayland_version.gni holds the minimum system libwayland versions for
  use_system_libwayland. It is maintained by hand and is independent of the
  in-tree version.

This is updated by an autoroller that tracks upstream release tags. A roll
normally only needs to update DEPS. If a roll fails:
- Add any new upstream sources to BUILD.gn.
- If upstream changed its configuration checks, regenerate include/config.h:
  $ apt-get install meson
  $ vpython3 third_party/wayland/generate_configs.py
